[Term]
id: CL:4306426
name: pinealocyte (Mmus)
def: "A pinealocyte of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cngb3 (Mmus), Ush2a (Mmus). It is glutamatergic. These cells are located in the brain , in or close to the regions: third ventricle . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4606 Pineal Crx Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z, https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1600-079x.1996.tb00284.x, https://doi.org/10.3389/fendo.2019.00590]
